  "Cars are normal goods. What will happen to the equilibrium price and quantity of cars if car dealers accept lower commissions, cars become cheaper, more firms start producing music cars, and households experience an increase in income?\nA. Price will fall and the effect on quantity is ambiguous.\nB. Price will rise and the effect on quantity is ambiguous.\nC. Quantity will fall and the effect on price is ambiguous.\nD. Quantity will rise and the effect on price is ambiguous.\nD",
