  "What is the consumer price index?\nA. Is not very useful as a measure of the cost of living.\nB. Is a perfect measure of the cost of living.\nC. Is a useful measure, but not a perfect measure, of the cost of living.\nD. Is not used as a measure of the cost of living.\nC",
  "Given the price increase of model rocket engines from $1.50 in 1972 to $ 2.50 today, which set of CPIs would align the prices when adjusted for inflation?\nA. 96 for 1972 and 154 for today\nB. 90 for 1972 and 150 for today\nC. 60 for 1972 and 95 for today\nD. 60 for 1972 and 120 for today\nA",
  "Which of the following is correct?\nA. The economy's two most important financial markets are the investment market and the saving market.\nB. The economy's two most important financial markets are the bond market and the stock market.\nC. The economy's two most important financial markets are banks and the stock market.\nD. The economy's two most important financial markets are financial markets and financial institutions.\nB",
